WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.222
Do not rewrite every query automatically.

00:00:03.222 --> 00:00:05.777
Rewriting is a corrective action.

00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:09.142
First, try the user's original wording.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.362
Retrieve evidence and grade it.

00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:15.562
If the evidence is already strong, proceed to generation.

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:19.490
Rewriting a good query may actually make retrieval worse.

00:00:19.954 --> 00:00:23.546
If evidence is weak, then rewrite and try again.

00:00:23.546 --> 00:00:26.926
Before another rewrite, ask three questions.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.351
Did the query actually change?

00:00:29.351 --> 00:00:32.391
Did the retrieved source I D's change?

00:00:32.391 --> 00:00:36.121
Is the missing fact even available in this source?

00:00:36.121 --> 00:00:41.921
If the same query keeps returning the same chunks, another rewrite may not help.

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:44.029
Maybe you need a different source.

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:47.701
Correction should respond to a diagnosed problem.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:51.942
Do not add a loop just because the architecture diagram has one.
